shots:
- index: 0
  duration_s: 2.5
  visual_anchor: <<<image_1>>>
  prompt: 'sb_001 0.0-2.5s. Use storyboard anchor <<<image_1>>> with <<<element_embry>>>,
    <<<element_kai>>>, and <<<element_kahaluu_lava_reef>>>. Embry and Kai wait outside
    the lineup instead of cutting across it. Heat, glare, and the public reef break
    establish that the stolen sick day still has rules. Camera stays waterline, slow
    observational drift with the swell, no dramatic push; composition: Embry and Kai
    are framed as part of a shared lineup; reef shapes occupy the lower foreground.
    Acting beats: Embry scans the lineup and chooses not to rush. Kai watches the
    reef and the locals before giving any cue. Both characters show autonomy through
    restraint rather than speech. Keep faces identity-readable and preserve public
    reef lineup etiquette. Native ambience and foley only unless voice status is later
    accepted.'
  voice_status: NO_DIALOGUE
  cinematography:
    shot_size: WS
    lens: wide water-housing perspective, approximately 24-35mm equivalent
    camera_mount: water-housed action or cinema camera for the waterline plate; shore
      safety B-camera optional
    camera_movement: slow observational drift with the swell, no dramatic push
    composition: Embry and Kai are framed as part of a shared lineup; reef shapes
      occupy the lower foreground.
    focus_behavior: identity-readable faces, no spray/glare occlusion
    lighting: hard coastal glare softened by water spray
    color_grade: realistic coastal daylight, clear water, dark lava reef
    atmosphere: hot humid Kona surf glare, salt spray, public lineup pressure
    temporal_pacing: four restrained 2.5 second beats within a 10 second dry run
    environment_lock: Kahaluu Bay / Kona Coast public lava reef break
    director_note: Embry keeps agency; Kai remains restrained, not a rescuer.
- index: 1
  duration_s: 2.5
  visual_anchor: <<<image_2>>>
  prompt: 'sb_002 2.5-5.0s. Use storyboard anchor <<<image_2>>> with <<<element_embry>>>,
    <<<element_kai>>>, and <<<element_kahaluu_lava_reef>>>. Embry''s phone buzzes
    from the beach bag as sweat and salt mark her face. Her palm skids on sun-softened
    wax, forcing her to reset her rail grip before the wave reaches the reef line.
    Camera stays low waterline close to the board rail, small handheld/swell movement
    tracking Embry''s grip reset; composition: Hands, rail, wax, Embry''s face, and
    reef line all remain legible. Acting beats: Embry notices the palm skid without
    melodrama. She resets her grip deliberately instead of pretending she is fine.
    The physical correction is the autonomy beat. Keep faces identity-readable and
    preserve public reef lineup etiquette. Native ambience and foley only unless voice
    status is later accepted.'
  voice_status: NO_DIALOGUE
  cinematography:
    shot_size: MS
    lens: moderate wide water-housing perspective, approximately 28-40mm equivalent
    camera_mount: water housing with close-focus capability; safety spotter required
      near reef
    camera_movement: small handheld/swell movement tracking Embry's grip reset
    composition: Hands, rail, wax, Embry's face, and reef line all remain legible.
    focus_behavior: identity-readable faces, no spray/glare occlusion
    lighting: bright glare off clear water with wet skin highlights
    color_grade: realistic coastal daylight, clear water, dark lava reef
    atmosphere: hot humid Kona surf glare, salt spray, public lineup pressure
    temporal_pacing: four restrained 2.5 second beats within a 10 second dry run
    environment_lock: Kahaluu Bay / Kona Coast public lava reef break
    director_note: Embry keeps agency; Kai remains restrained, not a rescuer.
- index: 2
  duration_s: 2.5
  visual_anchor: <<<image_3>>>
  prompt: 'sb_003 5.0-7.5s. Use storyboard anchor <<<image_3>>> with <<<element_embry>>>,
    <<<element_kai>>>, and <<<element_kahaluu_lava_reef>>>. Kai reads the local, the
    channel, the reef, and Embry''s paddle cadence. He holds position instead of taking
    the easy wave, then gives one restrained cue. Camera stays waterline, slightly
    outside the pair, gentle lateral drift that keeps Kai outside and Embry nearer
    the decision point; composition: Kai, Embry, channel, and shared lineup geometry
    are all visible. Acting beats: Kai conserves energy and waits. He notices the
    lineup first, then the channel, then Embry''s cadence. His cue is restrained;
    Embry keeps agency. Keep faces identity-readable and preserve public reef lineup
    etiquette. Native ambience and foley only unless voice status is later accepted.
    Text-only cue, not live voiced audio: Kai: If we paddle now, we''re cutting across
    the lineup.'
  voice_status: VOICE_TEXT_ONLY
  cinematography:
    shot_size: MWS
    lens: wide-to-normal water-housing perspective, approximately 30-45mm equivalent
    camera_mount: water housing with operator outside the path; optional shore lens
      for continuity
    camera_movement: gentle lateral drift that keeps Kai outside and Embry nearer
      the decision point
    composition: Kai, Embry, channel, and shared lineup geometry are all visible.
    focus_behavior: identity-readable faces, no spray/glare occlusion
    lighting: wet rashguard highlights and high water glare
    color_grade: realistic coastal daylight, clear water, dark lava reef
    atmosphere: hot humid Kona surf glare, salt spray, public lineup pressure
    temporal_pacing: four restrained 2.5 second beats within a 10 second dry run
    environment_lock: Kahaluu Bay / Kona Coast public lava reef break
    director_note: Embry keeps agency; Kai remains restrained, not a rescuer.
- index: 3
  duration_s: 2.5
  visual_anchor: <<<image_4>>>
  prompt: 'sb_004 7.5-10.0s. Use storyboard anchor <<<image_4>>> with <<<element_embry>>>,
    <<<element_kai>>>, and <<<element_kahaluu_lava_reef>>>. Embry chooses the safe
    channel and commits only when the lineup opens. The wave, reef, softened wax,
    and phone obligation converge into one visible decision. Camera stays waterline
    just inside the wave shoulder, brief forward glide with the shoulder as Embry
    chooses the safe line; composition: Embry, wave shoulder, reef boundary, and safe
